ref_dict.lemma9:
\begin{lemma}\label{lemma9}
    Take $q,Q,T\leq x^{\mathcal{O}(1)}$ with $q$ prime, take $P$ any polynomial, and write $\sum_{n,m}^{\sharp}$ for a sum subject to $n,m>q$ and $(nm,q)=1$. Then up to an error $\ll x^{\varepsilon}$
    \begin{align*}
        &\sum_{n,m \leq Q}^{\sharp} d_{3}(n)d_{3}(m)c_{q}(n-m)P(\log n/Q)P(\log m/Q)\hspace{0,9cm} \ll\ \frac{Q^2}{q}+q^{11/8}Q+q^{9/16}\sqrt{Q}, \\
        &\sum_{\substack{n\leq Q\\Q < m \leq T}}^{\sharp} \frac{d_{3}(n)d_{3}(m)c_{q}(n-m)P(\log n/Q)}{m^{2/3}} e\left((n/Q)^{1/3}\right)\hspace{0,4cm} \ll\  \frac{(Tx)^{1/3}}{q}\Big( \frac{QT^{1/3}}{q}+q^{11/8}Q^{1/3}+\frac{q^{9/16}}{Q^{1/6}}\Big),\\
        &\sum_{Q < n,m \leq T}^{\sharp} \frac{d_{3}(n)d_{3}(m)c_{q}(n-m)}{(nm)^{2/3}} e\left((n/Q)^{1/3} - (m/Q)^{1/3}\right) \ll \frac{(Tx)^{2/3}}{q^2} \Big( \frac{T^{2/3}}{q}+\frac{q^{11/8}}{Q^{1/3}}+\frac{q^{9/16}}{Q^{5/6}}\Big).
    \end{align*}
\end{lemma}

ref_dict.bound of L^3:
\begin{lemma}\label{bound of L^3}
Let $\chi$ be a primitive Dirichlet character modulo $q$. For $y > 1$ and $T \geq 2$, the second moment of $L$-functions on the critical line satisfies the following bound:
\[
\int_{y}^{T} \frac{|L(1/2 + it, \chi)|^2}{t} \, dt \ll\left(1 + \frac{q^{1/3}}{y^{2/3}} + \frac{q^{1/2}}{y}\right)\log^5(qT).
\]
\end{lemma}

